# Build scratch (the prebuilt payloads in out/ and truehd-out/ ARE committed)
*.ipk
build/

# OS cruft
.DS_Store

# dts2lpcm/ — local-only investigation area, never part of the shipped tool.
# Path A (demuxer retag + in-pipeline converter) was REFUTED on hardware
# 2026-07-24: umediaserver validates the LPCM stream at pipeline SETUP, so DTS
# bytes relabelled audio/x-private-ts-lpcm fail with errorCode 100 before the
# converter ever runs. Nothing here shipped and nothing here should be committed
# — the binaries are on-device-refuted, so .claude/rules/releasing.md bars them
# outright. The full 15 MB (binaries + regenerable desktop-validation fixtures)
# is archived out-of-repo at dts_restore_work/dts2lpcm-archive/; the working
# copy of the design/runbook record stays here, untracked.
# The multichannel route that DOES work needs no plugin at all:
#   ffmpeg -c:v copy -c:a pcm_bluray -ar 48000 -ac 6 -f mpegts
#
# NOTE for future edits: keep ignores scoped like this. Do NOT add a bare `*.so`
# to this file — the shipped out/, truehd-out/ and demux-out/ binaries are
# tracked ON PURPOSE and rule #1 requires re-committing them after a rebuild, so
# a blanket ignore would make `git add` silently skip a rebuilt decoder.
dts2lpcm/
